Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• `country_region_code`: filter to the United States (`'US'`).  
• `country_region`     : (optional) human‑readable country name.  
• `date`                : restrict rows to the two study windows  
  – Period‑1  `'2019‑01‑01'  ≤ date < '2020‑01‑01'`  
  – Period‑2  `'2020‑01‑01'  ≤ date < '2021‑01‑01'`  
• `symptom_anxiety`     : cast to FLOAT64 and average.  
• `symptom_depression`  : cast to FLOAT64 and average.  


Conditions that will be applied  

1. `country_region_code = 'US'`  
2. `DATE(date)` between the required bounds (the column is STRING, so we CAST / PARSE it to DATE first).  


Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final BigQuery SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows) that progressively lead to the answer.  
Replace nothing—dataset and table names are already fully qualified.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at raw rows for the United States
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Distinct years available for the U.S. data
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM DATE(date)) AS yr
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Anxiety & depression values in 2019 for quick inspection
SELECT date,
       symptom_anxiety,
       symptom_depression
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
  AND DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Same as above but cast to FLOAT64
SELECT date,
       CAST(symptom_anxiety    AS FLOAT64) AS anxiety_val,
       CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64) AS depression_val
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
  AND DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Average anxiety & depression for Period‑1 (2019)
SELECT
  AVG(CAST(symptom_anxiety    AS FLOAT64)) AS avg_anxiety_2019,
  AVG(CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64)) AS avg_depression_2019
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
  AND DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Average anxiety & depression for Period‑2 (2020)
SELECT
  AVG(CAST(symptom_anxiety    AS FLOAT64)) AS avg_anxiety_2020,
  AVG(CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64)) AS avg_depression_2020
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
  AND DATE(date) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) A single query returning both period averages side‑by‑side
WITH stats AS (
  SELECT
    CASE
      WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31' THEN '2019'
      WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31' THEN '2020'
    END AS yr,
    CAST(symptom_anxiety    AS FLOAT64) AS anx,
    CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64) AS dep
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
  WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
    AND DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
)
SELECT
  yr,
  AVG(anx) AS avg_anxiety,
  AVG(dep) AS avg_depression
FROM stats
GROUP BY yr
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Compute the percentage increase using conditional aggregation
SELECT
  AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_anxiety AS FLOAT64) END) AS avg_anxiety_2019,
  AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_anxiety AS FLOAT64) END) AS avg_anxiety_2020,
  AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64) END) AS avg_depression_2019,
  AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64) END) AS avg_depression_2020
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Same as #8 but add percentage deltas
SELECT
  avg_anxiety_2019,
  avg_anxiety_2020,
  100 * (avg_anxiety_2020 - avg_anxiety_2019) / avg_anxiety_2019 AS pct_increase_anxiety,
  avg_depression_2019,
  avg_depression_2020,
  100 * (avg_depression_2020 - avg_depression_2019) / avg_depression_2019 AS pct_increase_depression
FROM (
  SELECT
    AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_anxiety AS FLOAT64) END) AS avg_anxiety_2019,
    AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_anxiety AS FLOAT64) END) AS avg_anxiety_2020,
    AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64) END) AS avg_depression_2019,
    AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64) END) AS avg_depression_2020
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
  WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final neatly‑formatted answer with one row per symptom
WITH base AS (
  SELECT
    AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_anxiety AS FLOAT64) END) AS anx_2019,
    AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_anxiety AS FLOAT64) END) AS anx_2020,
    AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64) END) AS dep_2019,
    AVG(CASE WHEN DATE(date) BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-12-31' THEN CAST(symptom_depression AS FLOAT64) END) AS dep_2020
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_symptom_search.symptom_search_country_weekly`
  WHERE country_region_code = 'US'
)
SELECT 'anxiety'    AS symptom,
       anx_2019     AS avg_2019,
       anx_2020     AS avg_2020,
       100*(anx_2020 - anx_2019)/anx_2019 AS pct_increase
FROM base
UNION ALL
SELECT 'depression',
       dep_2019,
       dep_2020,
       100*(dep_2020 - dep_2019)/dep_2019
FROM base
LIMIT 20;
```
